WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.964 --> 00:00:20.191
The shook the gates in front of the castle.

2
00:00:20.211 --> 00:00:23.352
"It's late," Gerald explained.

3
00:00:23.372 --> 00:00:26.373
"There's another way into this hotel.

4
00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:28.254
But you have to climb through a hole."

5
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:33.076
"The ladies won't like that," said the middle-aged gentleman.

6
00:00:34.732 --> 00:00:36.833
But the ladies said they loved adventures.

7
00:00:36.854 --> 00:00:39.495
"Such a thrill!"

8
00:00:39.996 --> 00:00:41.997
said the one in the hat with flowers.

9
00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:47.140
So they went along the road until they came to the hole in the bushes.

10
00:00:48.141 --> 00:00:49.962
Gerald went first with a lantern.

11
00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:53.004
Next it was Mabel's turn.

12
00:00:54.365 --> 00:00:57.107
Then all the creatures slid down into the cave.

13
00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:04.512
They followed Gerald into the arched tunnel and out onto the terrace.

14
00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:09.853
"Oh!" The creatures admired the view in the moonlight.

15
00:01:12.494 --> 00:01:16.115
They continued along the gravel paths toward the Temple of Flora.

16
00:01:17.175 --> 00:01:21.376
Gerald's plan was to hide the creatures in the passage until the charm broke.

17
00:01:23.897 --> 00:01:27.918
Suddenly Gerald saw the statue of Hermes leap from his pedestal.

18
00:01:28.858 --> 00:01:30.339
Gerald was still wearing the ring.

19
00:01:31.239 --> 00:01:34.760
He knew that he was the only one who could see Hermes coming toward them.

20
00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:38.057
Gerald slipped the ring from his finger.

21
00:01:38.958 --> 00:01:42.260
The statue was back on its pedestal, still as could be.

22
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.442
When Gerald put the ring back on, Hermes was circling the Ugly-Wuglies.

23
00:01:47.462 --> 00:01:55.027
"This is a very superior hotel," said an Ugly-Wugly wearing a top hat.

24
00:01:55.047 --> 00:01:57.308
"The grounds are beautiful."

25
00:01:57.328 --> 00:02:01.851
"We'll have to enter through the back door," Mabel said.

26
00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:04.252
"The front door is locked early."

27
00:02:05.212 --> 00:02:06.213
"What an adventure!"

28
00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.814
muttered a short Ugly-Wugly in a cap.

29
00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.994
"I feel young again!"

30
00:02:12.615 --> 00:02:15.296
They hurried up the steps of the Temple of Flora.

31
00:02:16.377 --> 00:02:18.518
Mabel went behind the statue of the goddess.

32
00:02:19.558 --> 00:02:21.219
Gerald's lantern lit up a door.

33
00:02:21.239 --> 00:02:24.180
"This way," said Mabel.

34
00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.762
"You lead the way," said the middle-aged gentleman to Gerald.

35
00:02:30.742 --> 00:02:35.445
"Uh I I must stay behind to close the door," said Gerald.

36
00:02:36.445 --> 00:02:38.367
"You wouldn't want us to get in trouble, would you?"

37
00:02:39.248 --> 00:02:41.429
The creatures agreed they didn't want that.

38
00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.011
"Here, you take the lantern."

39
00:02:44.852 --> 00:02:47.053
Gerald handed it to the middle-aged gentleman.

40
00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:50.696
"I wish you a pleasant stay in the very nice hotel."

41
00:02:52.257 --> 00:02:55.900
One by one the other creatures followed their leader into the passage.

42
00:02:56.841 --> 00:03:00.744
Waiting outside, Mabel and Gerald hardly dared to breathe.

43
00:03:01.756 --> 00:03:04.997
But before they could shut the door, there was a scuffling noise.

44
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:07.738
The creatures were trying to escape!

45
00:03:09.818 --> 00:03:12.019
Mabel and Gerald struggled to close the door.

46
00:03:12.039 --> 00:03:15.400
"Oh, I can't push anymore!"

47
00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:16.680
cried Mabel.

48
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.861
"They mustn't get out!"

49
00:03:19.361 --> 00:03:20.081
said Gerald.

50
00:03:20.101 --> 00:03:22.622
"What's going on?"

51
00:03:23.122 --> 00:03:25.003
said a new voice behind the children.

52
00:03:25.023 --> 00:03:27.104
"Help us!"

53
00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:28.404
cried Gerald.

54
00:03:29.412 --> 00:03:32.273
A man stepped in and helped the children shut the door.

55
00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:38.556
you," said Mabel breathlessly.

56
00:03:38.576 --> 00:03:40.317
"Who are you?"

57
00:03:40.337 --> 00:03:43.098
"I've come from London."

58
00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:44.859
The man paused.

59
00:03:45.719 --> 00:03:47.420
"To be the caretaker of this estate.

60
00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.301
Now tell me what this is all about.

61
00:03:51.041 --> 00:03:52.602
Who were those strange people?"

62
00:03:52.622 --> 00:03:57.584
"If we told you the truth, you wouldn't believe us," said Gerald.

63
00:03:58.632 --> 00:04:01.133
"Remember, I saw them," said the man.

64
00:04:01.153 --> 00:04:04.594
"Tell him," Mabel urged Gerald.

65
00:04:05.554 --> 00:04:08.415
So Gerald told the whole story of the magic ring.

66
00:04:08.435 --> 00:04:12.796
"We think the creatures will turn back into old coats tomorrow.

67
00:04:13.236 --> 00:04:14.416
Then we can take them home.

68
00:04:14.796 --> 00:04:15.997
Do you believe any of this?"

69
00:04:16.017 --> 00:04:20.018
"No." The man shook his head.

70
00:04:21.018 --> 00:04:23.019
It was time for the children to go home.

71
00:04:23.039 --> 00:04:27.160
"Don't open that door," Gerald warned the man.

72
00:04:28.264 --> 00:04:30.546
"Wait for us to come back tomorrow at ten o'clock."

73
00:04:35.649 --> 00:04:38.911
The next morning the four children returned to the Temple of Flora.

74
00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.812
Everything was quiet.

75
00:04:40.832 --> 00:04:44.135
"Look!" Kathleen cried.

76
00:04:44.935 --> 00:04:46.276
She pointed to the floor.

77
00:04:47.217 --> 00:04:49.818
The caretaker lay there, moaning softly.

78
00:04:53.969 --> 00:04:58.243
At the same time, an Ugly-Wugly was peering at them through the bushes.
